  "result": "I added `click.KeyValue`. `@click.option('--set', type=click.KeyValue())` now turns `key=value` into a `(key, value)` tuple. The new tests pass along with the rest of `tests/test_types.py`. I didn't run the full suite.\n\n- **Parsing:** it splits on the first `=`, so `a=b=c` gives `('a', 'b=c')`. An empty value is allowed: `a=` gives `('a', '')`.\n- **Errors:** input with no `=` (such as `novalue`) or an empty key (such as `=value`) fails with `'\u2026' is not a valid key=value pair.` The empty string `\"\"` fails the same way.\n- **Where:** the class is in `src/click/types.py` and is exported from `src/click/__init__.py`. Its type name is `key_value`.\n- **Tests:** I added them at the end of `tests/test_types.py`. They cover the valid cases and the three invalid inputs above.\n\nDuring the work I made one stray edit call to a path that doesn't exist. It failed and changed nothing.",
